Offline launches requested by the launcher

`xodus-cli run --offline` (requires --license-cache): the launcher already
found Microsoft unreachable, so the launch skips the device-credential
renewal, the ticket and content-license requests and the PlayFab
authorisation outright and starts on the stored offline license, which is
held to the same rules as after a failed request. The Wine process gets
XODUS_FORCE_OFFLINE=1 so the runtime signs in from its cached identity at
once. A launch with a license cache but without the flag now survives a
failed device-credential renewal (the device token expires while offline)
and lets the content-license step decide instead of failing before it.

